{
  "description": "Item-line amount rule shared by the ClientLedger client (cl-model forms::item_lines) and the engine (U-85, PR-A). Synthetic. amount = round(quantity x unitPrice, 2), half away from zero (decimal.js ROUND_HALF_UP, precision 40). quantity: > 0 and < 100000000, at most 4 decimals. unitPrice: >= 0, at most 4 decimals. A quantity with an amount and no unitPrice is allowed (process review S2); a unitPrice without a quantity is not. Valid cases give the exact amount; invalid cases give a reason code. A zero amount is a valid rounding result here; the client still refuses a line whose amount is not more than zero.",
  "reasons": {
    "quantity_not_positive": "quantity is zero or less",
    "quantity_out_of_range": "quantity has more than 8 integer digits (>= 100000000)",
    "quantity_too_precise": "quantity has more than 4 decimals",
    "rate_negative": "unitPrice is below zero",
    "rate_too_precise": "unitPrice has more than 4 decimals",
    "quantity_required": "unitPrice without a quantity",
    "amount_out_of_range": "quantity x unitPrice leaves numeric(19,4)"
  },
